# ai-dev — local AI development stack (FETCHED-ONLINE, never baked). Ollama (the
# local LLM server) plus terminal AI coding clients. The members listed here are
# the CLIENTS + the BASE ollama package; the CORRECT ollama variant for the
# machine's GPU is chosen at install time by PCI detection in ai-dev.d/post-add
# (NVIDIA → ollama-cuda, AMD → ollama-rocm, otherwise plain ollama) — that
# detection MUST live in the hook, where PCI is real, NOT in this manifest.
#
# `ollama` is listed as the official-repo baseline so the pack is never empty and
# a machine with no discrete GPU still gets a working server; the hook installs
# the matching accelerated variant ON TOP for NVIDIA/AMD. `aider-chat` is AUR
# (the engine bootstraps paru for it); `aichat` is official-repo.
#
# AI provider wiring: the upstream Quickshell AI service (Super+I) AUTO-DISCOVERS
# running local Ollama models at runtime (services/Ai.qml → show-installed-ollama
# -models.sh queries `localhost:11434`); it reads its config from the synced
# ~/.config/quickshell/ii tree, which is rsync --delete territory we must NEVER
# write. There is no verifiable user-owned provider file outside that tree to
# point at ollama, so per PROPOSAL §7's audit fix the hook installs ollama +
# clients and prints a documented manual-setup hint instead of writing a provider
# file. Pull a model (`ollama pull …`) and the Super+I picker lists it.
#meta:type dev
ollama
aider-chat
aichat
